DATA[847.36]=[
(847.36,'gṛhā vai pratiṣṭhā sūktaṁ tat pratiṣṭhitatamayā vācā śaṁstavyaṁ','The hymn is a house, a firm foundation; it should be recited with speech that is most firmly established.','gṛhā:houses or shelter;vai:indeed;pratiṣṭhā:firm foundation;sūktaṁ:hymn;tat:that;pratiṣṭhitatamayā:most firmly established;vācā:with speech;śaṁstavyaṁ:to be recited or praised'),
(854.079,'tasmād yady api dūra iva paśūn labhate gṛhān evainān ājigamiṣati gṛhā hi paśūnāṁ pratiṣṭhā','Therefore, even if one obtains cattle far away, one wishes to bring them to the houses; houses are the firm shelter of cattle.','tasmād:therefore;yady:if;api:even;dūra:far;iva:as if;paśūn:cattle;labhate:obtains;gṛhān:to houses;evainān:indeed these, eva plus enan;ājigamiṣati:wishes to bring here;gṛhā:houses;hi:indeed;paśūnāṁ:of cattle;pratiṣṭhā:firm shelter'),
(866.32,'pratiṣṭhā uttamā pratiṣṭhā','A firm foundation; the highest foundation.','pratiṣṭhā:firm foundation;uttamā:highest'),
(869.76,'tad daivaṁ kṣatraṁ sā śrīs tad ādhipatyaṁ tad bradhnasya viṣṭapaṁ tat prajāpater āyatanaṁ','That is divine sovereignty, that is prosperity, that is lordship; that is the bright sun’s abode, that is Prajapati’s dwelling.','tad:that;daivaṁ:divine;kṣatraṁ:sovereignty;sā:that;śrīs:prosperity, sandhi of shrih;ādhipatyaṁ:lordship;bradhnasya:of the bright one or sun;viṣṭapaṁ:abode;tat:that;prajāpater:of Prajapati;āyatanaṁ:dwelling'),
(882.56,'tat svārājyaṁ ṛdhnoti etam evaitābhir ityādi pratiṣṭhā api gṛhāṇāṁ pratiṣṭhā uttamā pratiṣṭhā','That is independent rule; it prospers this one through these—“and so forth”; the speaker returns to foundation, the foundation of houses, and the highest foundation.','tat:that;svārājyaṁ:independent rule;ṛdhnoti:prospers;etam:this one;evaitābhir:indeed through these, eva plus etabhih;ityādi:and so forth;pratiṣṭhā:foundation;api:also, recorded return fragment;gṛhāṇāṁ:of houses;uttamā:highest')]
